WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.047
Look around you. Computers are everywhere.

2
00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:10.982
Some are easy to see. Some are
hiding inside other things.

3
00:00:11.482 --> 00:00:17.473
A computer is a machine that runs
programs. Computers come in lots of sizes.

4
00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:24.195
A desktop, a laptop, a tablet and a
smartphone. All four are computers.

5
00:00:24.695 --> 00:00:28.688
People use computers for lots of
different jobs. Here are five.

6
00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:32.484
Talking to Grandma far
away. That is communication.

7
00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:36.698
Watching a film, or playing a
game. That is entertainment.

8
00:00:36.918 --> 00:00:40.448
Drawing a picture, or making
music. That is creativity.

9
00:00:40.668 --> 00:00:43.454
Finding out about lions. That is research.

10
00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:48.411
And controlling other machines, like
a washing machine. That is control.

11
00:00:48.911 --> 00:00:54.716
One tablet can run lots of different programs.
A program on a tablet is called an app.

12
00:00:54.936 --> 00:00:56.747
Open Paint, and you can draw.

13
00:00:56.967 --> 00:00:59.382
Open the ball game, and you can play.

14
00:00:59.602 --> 00:01:02.342
Open Writing, and you can type a story.

15
00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:07.252
Videos plays films. Call rings
Grandma. Search finds things out.

16
00:01:07.472 --> 00:01:13.742
Six programs, and just one computer.
A computer can run many programs.

17
00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:19.257
A computer needs information to work
with. It goes in through an input.

18
00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:24.307
A keyboard puts letters in. A mouse
puts in your pointing and clicking.

19
00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:28.335
A microphone puts your voice
in. A camera puts a picture in.

20
00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.759
When you tap a touchscreen,
your tap goes in too.

21
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:35.882
Then the computer gives
information out, through an output.

22
00:01:36.102 --> 00:01:40.281
A screen shows words and
pictures. A speaker plays sounds.

23
00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:45.285
A printer puts them on paper. Lights
can flash to tell you something.

24
00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:50.520
A touchscreen is both. Your tap
goes in, and the picture comes out.

25
00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:58.079
A computer does not have to look like a computer. Lots
of everyday machines have a small one hiding inside.

26
00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:03.686
A washing machine has one. It
controls the wash: fill, wash, spin.

27
00:02:03.906 --> 00:02:07.575
Traffic lights have one. It
decides when each light changes.

28
00:02:07.795 --> 00:02:11.556
A microwave, a car, a watch
and a TV have one too.

29
00:02:11.776 --> 00:02:16.745
A spoon, a book and a candle have none.
Nothing inside them decides what they do.

30
00:02:17.245 --> 00:02:23.329
A robot is a machine with a computer inside.
Its program makes it move and do a job.

31
00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:26.382
In a factory, a robot arm builds cars.

32
00:02:26.602 --> 00:02:31.014
At home, a robot vacuum cleans the
floor, then goes back to charge.

33
00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:34.717
On Mars, a rover drives
about and takes pictures.

34
00:02:34.937 --> 00:02:39.627
Robots also work in hospitals and
warehouses, and even under the sea.

35
00:02:39.847 --> 00:02:42.680
Most robots do not look
like people at all.

36
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.590
A bicycle moves too, but it is not a
robot. It moves because you pedal it.

37
00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:53.756
So now you know. Computers do lots of jobs,
and one computer can run many programs.

38
00:02:53.976 --> 00:02:59.502
Information goes in, and it comes out.
And computers hide inside everyday things.

39
00:02:59.722 --> 00:03:03.112
A robot has a computer
inside that makes it move.

40
00:03:03.332 --> 00:03:05.933
Now go and find the computers around you.
